The closing phrase in Lecture 124 should be preserved: TRE teaches entrepreneurs how to make money in and on real estate. The transcript does not define that phrase as a formal taxonomy, so the safest reconstruction is $C_{\text{stack}}
\approx
C_{\mathrm{in}}\cup C_{\mathrm{on}},$ where $C_{\mathrm{in}}$ includes brokerage-facing capabilities and $C_{\mathrm{on}}$ includes adjacent real-estate activities such as investing or wholesaling. The approximation sign is important. The book should use the phrase as a source-backed operating frame, not as legal, tax, or investment advice.

